      "per_the_northwestern_local_news_initia": "Per the Northwestern Local News Initiative + UNC Hussman School: the US lost more than 2,500 daily + weekly newspapers between 2005 and 2024 — roughly one-third of US local newsrooms. About 70 million Americans now live in \"news deserts\" or \"limited-news areas\" — counties with no local newspaper. Maine has lost smaller weeklies in many rural counties; the surviving papers have cut newsroom staff dramatically. The civic + democratic consequences of this collapse are still being measured.",
